WEBVTT

1
00:00:25.833 --> 00:00:30.000


2
00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:36.791
<b>Lord Krishna now moves away from</b>
<b>discussing the soul and explains to Arjuna:</b>

3
00:00:36.791 --> 00:00:38.250
<b>"Arjuna,</b>

4
00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:44.041
<b>even if you look at this from the perspective</b>
<b>of your Swadharma, that is your duties,</b>

5
00:00:44.041 --> 00:00:48.000
<b>you should not waver from this war.</b>

6
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:49.666
<b>For a Kshatriya like you,</b>

7
00:00:49.666 --> 00:00:55.791
<b>what could be more righteous than fighting</b>
<b>wholeheartedly in this dharmic war?"</b>

8
00:00:56.458 --> 00:01:00.708


9
00:01:00.708 --> 00:01:03.708
<b>Lord Krishna here speaks of Swadharma</b>

10
00:01:03.708 --> 00:01:12.291
<b>the duties that come naturally to you,</b>
<b>according to your nature.</b>

11
00:01:12.291 --> 00:01:15.666
<b>This is not determined by birth.</b>

12
00:01:15.666 --> 00:01:17.708
<b>Arjuna has the nature of a Kshatriya,</b>

13
00:01:17.708 --> 00:01:21.333
<b>and for him, Swadharma means to fight.</b>

14
00:01:21.333 --> 00:01:23.541
<b>And this is indeed a golden opportunity.</b>

15
00:01:23.541 --> 00:01:28.708
<b>This war of Mahabharata is for establishing</b>
<b>dharma, a war to uphold righteousness.</b>

16
00:01:28.708 --> 00:01:31.333
<b>Fighting for such a noble cause</b>

17
00:01:31.333 --> 00:01:36.333
<b>should be a matter of fortune and enthusiasm</b>
<b>for a Kshatriya like Arjuna.</b>

18
00:01:36.333 --> 00:01:38.375
<b>Why hesitate?</b>

19
00:01:38.375 --> 00:01:44.375
<b>It is through selflessly performing one's duties</b>
<b>that a person rises to higher consciousness.</b>

20
00:01:44.375 --> 00:01:47.250
<b>Here, Krishna wants to tell Arjuna</b>

21
00:01:47.250 --> 00:01:54.416
<b>that his thoughts of living in the forest and</b>
<b>begging for alms are inappropriate</b>

22
00:01:54.416 --> 00:01:56.375
<b>these paths are not meant for you.</b>

23
00:01:56.375 --> 00:02:00.958
<b>For you, this war should be inspiring</b>

24
00:02:00.958 --> 00:02:03.250
<b>a war for protecting dharma,</b>

25
00:02:03.250 --> 00:02:05.708
<b>for the welfare of society.</b>

26
00:02:06.416 --> 00:02:10.250


27
00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:12.166
<b>Dharma,</b>

28
00:02:12.166 --> 00:02:15.708
<b>this word has many meanings.</b>

29
00:02:15.708 --> 00:02:20.791
<b>One of them is that duty which you have chosen</b>

30
00:02:20.791 --> 00:02:25.083
<b>according to your nature, your innate disposition.</b>

31
00:02:25.083 --> 00:02:28.666
<b>Everyone has some hidden talent.</b>

32
00:02:28.666 --> 00:02:30.916
<b>Some are good speakers,</b>

33
00:02:30.916 --> 00:02:33.000
<b>some are good administrators,</b>

34
00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:35.166
<b>some are good artists</b>

35
00:02:35.166 --> 00:02:36.708
<b>many people,</b>

36
00:02:36.708 --> 00:02:38.791
<b>many talents.</b>

37
00:02:38.791 --> 00:02:42.875
<b>No one person can do everything,</b>

38
00:02:42.875 --> 00:02:43.666
<b>but</b>

39
00:02:43.666 --> 00:02:47.958
<b>every person excels in some field.</b>

40
00:02:47.958 --> 00:02:49.166
<b>Sometimes</b>

41
00:02:49.166 --> 00:02:52.041
<b>these talents are on the surface,</b>

42
00:02:52.041 --> 00:02:53.541
<b>shining bright,</b>

43
00:02:53.541 --> 00:02:57.041
<b>manifesting in childhood itself.</b>

44
00:02:57.041 --> 00:02:58.375
<b>And sometimes,</b>

45
00:02:58.375 --> 00:03:02.041
<b>under the influence of society or family,</b>

46
00:03:02.041 --> 00:03:03.375
<b>they get suppressed, </b>

47
00:03:03.375 --> 00:03:05.916
<b>forgotten.</b>

48
00:03:05.916 --> 00:03:11.208
<b>It's extremely important in life to</b>
<b>recognize this talent.</b>

49
00:03:11.208 --> 00:03:16.625
<b>To know what it is that we excel at,</b>

50
00:03:16.625 --> 00:03:20.000
<b>what work gives us satisfaction,</b>

51
00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:23.416
<b>what work society needs,</b>

52
00:03:23.416 --> 00:03:24.291
<b>and</b>

53
00:03:24.291 --> 00:03:28.333
<b>what can sustain our livelihood.</b>

54
00:03:28.333 --> 00:03:31.791
<b>And once this talent is found,</b>

55
00:03:31.791 --> 00:03:32.708
<b>then</b>

56
00:03:32.708 --> 00:03:42.833
<b>using it to contribute to society becomes</b>
<b>one's dharma, one's duty.</b>

57
00:03:42.833 --> 00:03:44.916
<b>For example</b>

58
00:03:44.916 --> 00:03:49.541
<b>you excel at simplifying and</b>
<b>explaining any subject,</b>

59
00:03:49.541 --> 00:03:52.000
<b>you feel great satisfaction</b>

60
00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:56.833
<b>when someone quickly understands</b>
<b>what you've taught,</b>

61
00:03:56.833 --> 00:04:00.375
<b>society needs good teachers,</b>

62
00:04:00.375 --> 00:04:05.875
<b>and it's also a respectable means of livelihood.</b>

63
00:04:05.875 --> 00:04:07.000
<b>In such a case,</b>

64
00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:10.125
<b>it becomes your dharma</b>

65
00:04:10.125 --> 00:04:13.083
<b>to advance in the field of education.</b>

66
00:04:13.083 --> 00:04:18.458
<b>To contribute to others' lives through your talent.</b>

67
00:04:18.458 --> 00:04:25.416
<b>If you have found your dharma,</b>
<b>this duty, then pursue it.</b>

68
00:04:25.416 --> 00:04:28.166
<b>And if you haven't found it yet,</b>

69
00:04:28.166 --> 00:04:29.541
<b>then search for it.</b>

70
00:04:29.541 --> 00:04:33.458
<b>Ask yourself these four questions.</b>

71
00:04:33.458 --> 00:04:35.541
<b>What is it:</b>

72
00:04:35.541 --> 00:04:37.458
<b>That you excel at</b>

73
00:04:37.458 --> 00:04:40.375
<b>That brings you joy</b>

74
00:04:40.375 --> 00:04:42.791
<b>`That society needs</b>

75
00:04:42.791 --> 00:04:43.583
<b>And</b>

76
00:04:43.583 --> 00:04:47.750
<b>that can sustain your livelihood</b>

77
00:04:47.750 --> 00:04:51.333
<b>And once you find this dharma,</b>

78
00:04:51.333 --> 00:04:55.291
<b>make it your life's purpose.</b>

79
00:04:55.958 --> 00:05:00.166


80
00:05:00.166 --> 00:05:02.333
<b>It is natural,</b>

81
00:05:02.333 --> 00:05:09.125
<b>all parents want their children to be successful.</b>

82
00:05:09.125 --> 00:05:10.333
<b>But</b>

83
00:05:10.333 --> 00:05:18.708
<b>this situation becomes complex when we carry</b>
<b>a narrow definition of success,</b>

84
00:05:18.708 --> 00:05:24.666
<b>and this definition is typically influenced</b>
<b>by social perceptions.</b>

85
00:05:24.666 --> 00:05:29.666
<b>We begin to equate success with earning money,</b>

86
00:05:29.666 --> 00:05:30.375
<b>or</b>

87
00:05:30.375 --> 00:05:31.750
<b>with certain fields,</b>

88
00:05:31.750 --> 00:05:33.166
<b>certain positions</b>

89
00:05:33.166 --> 00:05:38.958
<b>that society has declared</b>
<b>prestigious in its definition.</b>

90
00:05:38.958 --> 00:05:40.375
<b>But</b>

91
00:05:40.375 --> 00:05:44.791
<b>is this thinking right?</b>

92
00:05:44.791 --> 00:05:49.000
<b>If you consider flying high</b>
<b>as the only measure of success,</b>

93
00:05:49.000 --> 00:05:53.291
<b>could a duck ever win?</b>

94
00:05:53.291 --> 00:05:54.750
<b>And conversely,</b>

95
00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:57.541
<b>the ability to swim continuously</b>

96
00:05:57.541 --> 00:06:03.166
<b>would be an unfair standard for</b>
<b>a bird meant to fly.</b>

97
00:06:03.166 --> 00:06:04.750
<b>Similarly,</b>

98
00:06:04.750 --> 00:06:07.541
<b>everyone has their own unique talent,</b>

99
00:06:07.541 --> 00:06:08.208
<b>and</b>

100
00:06:08.208 --> 00:06:13.833
<b>it's essential for parents to</b>
<b>understand their children's nature,</b>

101
00:06:13.833 --> 00:06:16.041
<b>recognize their talents,</b>

102
00:06:16.041 --> 00:06:16.958
<b>and</b>

103
00:06:16.958 --> 00:06:22.333
<b>then encourage and</b>
<b>support them to walk that path.</b>

104
00:06:22.333 --> 00:06:25.875
<b>Success's definition isn't so narrow</b>

105
00:06:25.875 --> 00:06:32.291
<b>that it should be bound by some amount</b>
<b>of money, some field, or some position.</b>

106
00:06:32.291 --> 00:06:36.416
<b>Rise above such narrow definitions.</b>

107
00:06:36.416 --> 00:06:39.041
<b>The true definition of success is</b>

108
00:06:39.041 --> 00:06:45.458
<b>to earn a living while contributing to</b>
<b>society according to one's talent.</b>

109
00:06:45.458 --> 00:06:48.666
<b>This isn't a competition.</b>

110
00:06:48.666 --> 00:06:52.958
<b>Know the difference between</b>
<b>success and competition.</b>

111
00:06:53.500 --> 00:06:57.708


112
00:06:57.708 --> 00:07:02.916
<b>Any workplace is a confluence of diverse talents.</b>

113
00:07:02.916 --> 00:07:06.583
<b>Many people, each with their own capabilities,</b>

114
00:07:06.583 --> 00:07:09.375
<b>each with their own skills.</b>

115
00:07:09.375 --> 00:07:12.916
<b>Your work is a means of life,</b>

116
00:07:12.916 --> 00:07:16.666
<b>crucial for sustaining your livelihood.</b>

117
00:07:16.666 --> 00:07:17.500
<b>But</b>

118
00:07:17.500 --> 00:07:19.250
<b>it's not necessary</b>

119
00:07:19.250 --> 00:07:24.291
<b>to carry it like a burden throughout your life.</b>

120
00:07:24.291 --> 00:07:32.416
<b>Try to discover what aligns with your nature,</b>

121
00:07:32.416 --> 00:07:34.333
<b>what you excel at,</b>

122
00:07:34.333 --> 00:07:38.375
<b>and what brings you satisfaction when doing it.</b>

123
00:07:38.375 --> 00:07:47.500
<b>It's not necessary that your current profession</b>
<b>meets all these criteria.</b>

124
00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:52.833
<b>Nor is it necessary to change</b>
<b>this profession immediately.</b>

125
00:07:52.833 --> 00:07:53.791
<b>But</b>

126
00:07:53.791 --> 00:08:02.500
<b>your self-reflection will surely help in</b>
<b>choosing the right work in the future.</b>

127
00:08:02.500 --> 00:08:03.625
<b>Meanwhile,</b>

128
00:08:03.625 --> 00:08:06.791
<b>alongside your current work,</b>

129
00:08:06.791 --> 00:08:14.541
<b>you can gradually progress on</b>
<b>this newly discovered path.</b>

130
00:08:14.541 --> 00:08:15.958
<b>But</b>

131
00:08:15.958 --> 00:08:19.708
<b>how to find this path?</b>

132
00:08:19.708 --> 00:08:22.916
<b>Here are some ways</b>

133
00:08:22.916 --> 00:08:28.375
<b>consult a well-wisher, a mentor, a friend.</b>

134
00:08:28.375 --> 00:08:31.541
<b>Ask yourself these questions too</b>

135
00:08:31.541 --> 00:08:34.750
<b>what work are you skilled at?</b>

136
00:08:34.750 --> 00:08:38.625
<b>What kind of challenges attract you?</b>

137
00:08:38.625 --> 00:08:44.458
<b>For what work do people place</b>
<b>complete trust in you?</b>

138
00:08:44.458 --> 00:08:45.791
<b>Keep searching,</b>

139
00:08:45.791 --> 00:08:49.166
<b>and the day you find this path,</b>

140
00:08:49.166 --> 00:08:53.375
<b>accept it as your dharma</b>
<b>and move forward on it.</b>

141
00:08:53.375 --> 00:09:00.083
<b>It may take time for this new path to</b>
<b>become a complete means of livelihood.</b>

142
00:09:00.083 --> 00:09:01.000
<b>But</b>

143
00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:08.541
<b>work that matches your nature and preference</b>
<b>will surely bring you unique satisfaction,</b>

144
00:09:08.541 --> 00:09:11.250
<b>will definitely bring you joy.</b>

